    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d488">

                <pb facs="0863" n="849" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg849"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to
                        the British Prime Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Churchill</hi>)<anchor n="62" xml:id="d488-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-28T13:25:00-04:00">28 September, 1944—1:25 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>624. Your 785.<anchor n="63" xml:id="d488-f2"/> I have read with great interest
                    your telegram from Field Marshal Smuts, and I think we are all in agreement with
                    him as to the necessity of having the U.S.S.R. as a fully accepted and equal <pb
                        facs="0864" n="850" xml:id="pg850"/> member of any association of the great
                    powers formed for the purpose of preventing international war.</p>
                <p>It should be possible to accomplish this by adjusting our differences through
                    compromise by all the parties concerned and this ought to tide things over for a
                    few years until the child learns how to toddle.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
